<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The fullscreen game theme, and the named theme the game Activity binds to.

    SDLActivity draws its own surface and the game draws through SDL3's GPU API, so there are no
    widgets to theme: AppTheme is the whole of it, and it stays exactly what it has always been.

    Theme.ZeroHour.Game exists so ZeroHourActivity can name the window it runs in instead of
    inheriting the <application> theme by omission. It adds nothing - the parent is AppTheme - so the
    fullscreen behaviour, and the fact that AppTheme is still what an activity without a theme gets,
    are both unchanged. Naming it is the point: a change to a presentation theme can no longer reach
    the game surface by accident, which is the failure this phase exists to prevent.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="AppTheme" parent="android:Theme.NoTitleBar.Fullscreen" />

    <style name="Theme.ZeroHour.Game" parent="AppTheme" />
</resources>
